<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karim Khan Zand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1779</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Karim Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karim Khan Zand was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand dynasty</a>, who ruled most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> after the collapse of Afsharid power, and died in 1779. He declined the title of shah and styled himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil">Vakil</a>, or regent. His rule is remembered for relative stability, moderation and building works in Shiraz, and the Zand Empire did not long survive him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand.jpg" alt="Karim Khan Zand" width="309" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karim_Khan-e_Zand.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
